            <ArticleTitle>Workers not getting help they need to navigate the health care system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Health advocacy services connect employees with advisers who can answer questions and provide advice about using the often-Byzantine health care system. The number of companies offering such services has remained stagnant at about 24% since 2013, according to Optum, and it's a minority of companies that provide other kinds of help for dealing with the health care system.</AbstractText>
